-Indel co-phasing in \toolname also compared favourably with that of \whatshap, which phases indels by default (Fig.~\ref{fig:benchmarks}). Adding indels raised the SNV switch error rate of \whatshap by 17--20\% (0.081\% to 0.097\% at 60$\times$), and its Hamming distance, which then also counts indels, from 2.7\% to 9.3\% at 60$\times$. With indels, corrected \toolname made 3.0--3.7-fold fewer SNV switch errors than \whatshap (591 versus 2,139 at 60$\times$) at 37--56\% of its Hamming distance (3.5\% versus 9.3\% at 60$\times$, both including indels), while \whatshap phased 2.4--4.5 percentage points more of the benchmark heterozygous indels (49.8\% versus 45.4\% at 60$\times$) and built 14--28\% longer blocks (Fig.~\ref{fig:benchmarks}e,f).
